From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] V4L2 cameras: the camera chosen in the session is the default
 camera

QMediaDevices::defaultVideoInput(), a QML MediaDevices and a QCamera made
without a device took the first camera of the kernel's list as the default
(qv4l2cameradevices.cpp, "first camera is default"), whatever camera the
person had chosen as the default in the session.

The session's default camera is the one the person chose (WirePlumber keeps it
as default.configured.video.source in the "default" metadata of PipeWire).
QDefaultCameraMonitor follows that key and the camera nodes (Video/Source,
whose api.v4l2.path is the /dev/videoN the V4L2 backend lists) through a
connection to PipeWire of its own, and QV4L2CameraDevices marks the camera of
that path as the default. Every camera stays listed, in the same order; only
isDefault moves, and videoInputsChanged is emitted when the choice changes
while the program runs. A camera a program was given or chose by itself is
never touched.

When the session's default cannot be found among the cameras (no PipeWire
session, the chosen camera unplugged or not a V4L2 device, a name that matches
none of them), the first camera stays the default as before and the reason is
said once in qt.multimedia.ffmpeg.v4l2cameradevices, not at every scan of /dev.
Nobody having chosen is not a failure: the first camera is the default, and
nothing is said.

tst_qpipewiredefaultcamera checks the choice from the session's events, the
pick among the devices, every reason, and the monitor without a session.

AI was leveraged.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
